  2953	## D248 · 2026-10-30 · What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one
  2954	
  2955	- Alex, on the census of duplicate and trivial questions: "我们的标准要收口"; then "你要不要深度的写好plan, 怎么测量，golden 是怎么，我们来解决这个问题；整体不能regress，你要秉持我们过往工程的原则，以及作为一个hedge fund analyst 到底怎么判断合并，去重，这个标准很重要，不能观点爆炸"; then, not following the plan's table, "我没理解每个难点，我需要一个一个和你过，你讲人话给我例子". Each boundary was put to him with an example and two options; his replies are quoted per row. Plan, census and review rounds: [question-identity plan](research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md) §0–§4, §11b, §12.
  2956	- The class ($0, `census/`): the sealed three-month run opened 69 questions in 59 days; Claude's reading of the first 50 (not reviewed by Alex) marks 12 duplicates and 10 that should not have opened, 5 borderline. Matching merged 39 of 122 candidates; the duplicates left are the collision judge's "distinct question in one matter" verdicts, "same question" verdicts blocked by a model-written period start, and twins never compared.
  2957	- Decided (the general rule under all seven: two questions are one when the same outcome settles both; they are kept apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on each separately):
  2958	  1. **One plan, several wordings** (H1, "A"): wordings of one plan whose final check is the same number are one question; two numbers that move on their own and are watched separately stay apart; a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it. A not-yet-signed deal is a yes/no signing question (D210; PRD 06 keeps number and event questions apart); whether it merges into the plan's amount question follows the same bet-separately test, judged per case in the gold (the Ohio lease guarantee against the cloud-customer total in v38). Narrows the standard §4 "another quantity in the same deal (a guarantee beside a financing)" sentence taken from D190; consistent with D210.
  2959	  2. **One event, several deadlines** (H2, "A"): while the earlier-deadline question is open, a later deadline is its evidence, not a new question; when the earlier one falls due unresolved and the matter is still live, the system opens the next-deadline successor with the merged evidence, without waiting for a new article (new work for pull mode, D14, D54).
  2960	  3. **One product generation, several milestones** (H3, "A"): one question per generation, asked at the step that brings revenue (shipments begin); sampling and launch are its evidence; only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's phase-3 data and its approval) are separate questions.
  2961	  4. **A company's own quantity by fiscal and by calendar year** (H4, "A"): only the fiscal year opens (PRD 06 ladder rule 5); a calendar-year estimate is evidence to the fiscal question, weighed lower when the years differ much.
  2962	  5. **A model-written period start** (H5, "A"): for event and policy questions it no longer blocks a merge; object, event and due day are still checked.
  2963	  6. **Small matters opened as questions** (H6, "A， A"): a question opens only when its scale can change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk; otherwise the statement is evidence. Done in this round together with the merge changes, each measured as its own arm, then together on the holdout. Narrows the standard §3 class C ("a sized, not yet completed stake or acquisition").
  2964	  7. **The same statement carried by several outlets** (H7, "A"): code treats pieces with the same original speaker, original day and figures as one; the judge sees it once with the outlet count; every piece is still stored. Changes D204's "both shown to the judge" for this case; the risk put to him with the question (a qualification such as "excluding China sales" hidden; D204's 8 of 40 wrong merges) is measured on the G3 gold before it is switched on, as is the accuracy of the original-speaker and original-day fields it relies on.
  2965	- Next, in this order: the signed standard page (§3 class C, §4 "same question, succession or another question") carries these rules, then a read-only Codex drift review; then the plan's step 1 (structured census, the fixed-extraction replay harness, gold G1–G3, the September holdout week on Alex's go).
