**Serious findings remain.** For example, Alex chose to show repeated reports as one item to the judge, but the plan still says that choice is pending and does not plan to implement or test it.

1. **Serious — H7 is recorded but not carried into the work or measurement.** [Plan line 236](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:236) records Alex’s choice A. Yet [line 193](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:193) says to wait for his answer, and [line 135](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:135) says G3 will only measure the existing labels and change nothing. [D248](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2964) records the chosen display change and requires measuring the risk that a distinct qualification is hidden before switching it on. The plan has neither that implementation arm nor that measurement.

2. **Serious — the updated standard would omit an approved change.** [Plan lines 102 and 238](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:102) say to update section 4 of the signed standard. [D248](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2963) says H6 narrows the opening definition in **section 3, class C**, and [its next-step instruction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2965) explicitly names both section 3 and section 4. Updating only section 4 would leave the old class-C definition in the ruler used by gold and prompts.

3. **Serious — E’s acceptance can still miss a lost required question, and the final holdout is not specified for changed extraction.** [Plan line 189](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:189) now aligns fresh outputs by research matter and reads every *emitted* candidate, addressing part of round 12. But its stated no-loss condition covers only required items already in the extraction gold. A required matter proposed by the control but absent from the new answer, outside that gold, has no stated stopping condition. Further, [lines 140 and 190](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:140) freeze the holdout’s extraction answers yet score the combined configuration including E, which changes extraction. The fixed-candidate G1 cannot by itself score E’s new or missing outputs. This concerns the extraction change’s regression, not losses common to both matching arms.

4. **Serious — G1’s stated material is too narrow to judge its “worth opening” field.** [Plan lines 115 and 130](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:115) ask the gold to decide worth using the matching request. That request contains the candidate and truncated evidence, not the complete article: [candidate construction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:56) limits its evidence text, and [the collision request](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:205) adds the existing cards and excerpts. The [signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:510) requires the reference to be written from the original article. The stored request is useful for judging what matching could see; it is insufficient as the sole source for the gold’s opening judgment.

The round-4 structural rule **does close its named matching cases**: it distinguishes identity from worth, checks successor questions and their evidence, and adds a future-expiry test. It can detect a wrong merge or a lost required *proposed* question when the candidate and expected destination are in G1. The E-arm gap above remains outside that fixed-input comparison.

I verified the census totals by rerunning its read-only script: sealed **122 candidates, 39 merges, 2 successions**; v38 **32, 12, 1**. I also confirmed the 20 shared evidence links and the stored same-article 2026/2027 spending pair; the latter is now recorded as a remaining succession error at [plan line 120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:119). The census verdict categories still parse reason text, as the plan discloses.

The guarantee/financing example is in both the [signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:318) and [collision prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1). The plan now correctly leaves its causal role and any conflict with D210 unproven. Section 11b and D248 agree on the recorded H1–H7 answers, but I could not independently verify the full questions Alex saw from the short “A” quotations alone. I did not verify every archived verdict or cost estimate, and did not edit files.

**Serious findings remain: yes.**
